            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0296" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 183.9 Brazil/2: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-21T20:00:00-05:00"
                            >December 21, 1918—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 22—3 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>89. For the Secretary of State. Embassy, Rio de Janeiro, urgently requests
                    information as to how invitations to Peace Conference will be issued and whether
                    less important Allied countries such as Brazil may participate on their own
                    invitation. Embassy also states that The Chamber of Deputies have asked
                    Brazilian Minister of Foreign Office whether Brazil has been invited. Da Gama
                    sent personal message to me stating he would be very much embarrassed by his
                    inability to answer inquiries and asked for your friendly assistance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
